Dear Finance Team,

The Australian Taxation Office (ATO) has processed your Business
Activity Statement (BAS) for the September 2026 quarter and
determined that you are eligible for a refund of AUD $21,845.63.

Refund Details:
  ABN: 84 664 219 884
  BAS Period: July - September 2026
  GST Credit: AUD $18,420.50
  PAYG Withholding Credit: AUD $2,895.13
  Fuel Tax Credit: AUD $530.00
  Total Refund: AUD $21,845.63

How the Refund Will Be Processed:

  The refund will be automatically deposited into the bank
  account you registered with the ATO when you set up your
  ABN. No action is required.

  If you need to update your bank account details:

  1. Log in to ATO Online Services:
     Navigate to online.services.ato.gov.au in your browser
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click links from emails.)

  2. Use myGovID or AUSkey to authenticate

  3. Go to Business → Account Details → Bank Account

  4. Update your bank account information

  Important Security Notes:
  The ATO will NEVER:
  - Send you a "Verify Bank Account" or "Claim Refund" link via email
  - Ask for BSB, account number, or SWIFT code through a portal
  - Request director's passport through email or third-party portals
  - Set a deadline for bank verification (refunds don't expire)
  - Cite "forfeiture" of refunds for non-verification

  Refunds are automatically deposited. There is no "Bank Account
  Verification Program" requiring email-based re-verification.

  If you receive an email asking you to "verify" or "claim" your
  refund through a link, it is a phishing attempt targeting
  Australian businesses.

  To check your refund status:
  1. Navigate to online.services.ato.gov.au manually
  2. Log in with myGovID
  3. Go to Activity Statements → Refund Status

  Or call the ATO business line: 13 28 66 (8am-6pm AEDT, Mon-Fri)

Common Questions:
  Q: Can refunds be sent to overseas bank accounts?
  A: Yes, if registered with the ATO. Update through ATO Online
     Services (navigate manually), not through email links.

  Q: What if my refund doesn't arrive?
  A: Check your refund status online, or call 13 28 66.
     Refunds are not "forfeited" for non-verification.

